  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The equation of the tangent at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;to the parabola is</p><p><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;</p><p>So, the slope of the normal to the circle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br />The equation of normal to the circle at <math><mi>Q</mi></math> will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br />The point <math><mi>Q</mi></math> is the intersection of the&nbsp;tangent at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;and the normal at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math></p><p>On solving the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>31</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>31</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>42</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, the coordinates of the point&nbsp;<math><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>31</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>42</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
